ysis are crucial for ensuring the validity of the results. Key assumptions include:\n\n1. **Linearity**: The relationship between the independent and dependent variables is linear.\n2. **Independence**: The residuals (errors) are independent of each other.\n3. **Homoscedasticity**: The variance of the residuals is constant across all levels of the independent variable(s).\n4. **Normality**: The residuals are normally distributed, particularly important for inference purposes.\n\nViolating these assumptions can lead to biased estimates, inefficient predictions, and invalid statistical inferences. For instance, if the assumption of homoscedasticity is violated (i.e., the residuals exhibit heteroscedasticity), the ESS may not accurately reflect the model's fit, leading to misleading conclusions about the relationship between variables.\n\nIn summary, the Error Sum of Squares is a vital measure in regression analysis that quantifies the difference between observed and predicted values. It plays a significant role in model optimization and evaluation, with its minimization being a key objective in regression modeling. Understanding the assumptions associated with ESS is essential for ensuring the reliability of regression results and making informed decisions based on the analysis.", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": [], "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null}, "content_filter_results": {"hate": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}, "protected_material_code": {"filtered": false, "detected": false}, "protected_material_text": {"filtered": false, "detected": false}, "self_harm": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}, "sexual": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}, "violence": {"filtered": false, "severity": "safe"}}}], "created": 1771166032, "model": "gpt-4o-mini-2024-07-18", "object": "chat.completion", "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": "fp_f97eff32c5", "usage": {"completion_tokens": 591, "prompt_tokens": 299, "total_